post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
covey is installed under /usr/share/covey. It does not start itself.
For your user:

  covey php configure 85
  covey install
  covey trust
  covey up

User services cannot bind port 80 until the unprivileged port floor is
lowered. The README has the sysctl command. Leave the system
caddy.service disabled; covey runs its own user unit.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'
covey was upgraded on disk. From your user, run:

  covey install

That reloads user units. Then "covey up" if the stack was running.
EOF
}

post_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Package files are gone. Per-user state is not: ~/.config/covey,
the ~/.local/share/covey symlink, user systemd units, the local CA,
and Docker volumes. The README uninstall section lists them.
~/Covey is your sites directory; removing the package does not touch it.
EOF
}
